She serves on the advisory board
of the Stanford Institute for

00:12:08.565 --> 00:12:14.096
Economic Policy Research, she is
involved with the School of Medicine and

00:12:14.096 --> 00:12:17.193
as a member of the GSPs Advisory Council.

00:12:17.193 --> 00:12:23.349
Where she is invariably the most involved,
enthusiastic and engaged participant in

00:12:23.349 --> 00:12:28.663
discussions about the school and
the future of business and leadership.

00:12:28.663 --> 00:12:32.164
Please join me in welcoming
new Noosheen Hashemi.

00:12:32.164 --> 00:12:34.930
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE] Good afternoon.

00:12:34.930 --> 00:12:40.347
Thank you Dean Levin,
faculty, family members and

00:12:40.347 --> 00:12:44.675
friends and hello MSX class of 2021.

00:12:44.675 --> 00:12:49.001
[APPLAUSE] It is a true
honor to be celebrating this

00:12:49.001 --> 00:12:52.970
important milestone with each of you.

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:55.923
Today marks the end of your
time as a GSB student and

00:12:55.923 --> 00:12:58.890
the beginning of your
journey as a proud GSB alum.

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:03.450
Not only will you feel deeply
connected to this venerable,

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:08.880
uniquely entrepreneurial and impact
focused institution for decades to come.

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:13.213
But you will also cherish the enduring
friendships that you have nurtured during

00:13:13.213 --> 00:13:14.670
your time here.

00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:18.450
I know these things to be true
from my personal experience.

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:22.585
While every class is
special in its own way,

00:13:22.585 --> 00:13:26.182
this class experienced
something truly extraordinary.

00:13:26.182 --> 00:13:29.084
A global pandemic that
upended our world and

00:13:29.084 --> 00:13:35.290
shut down even places of worship which
had remained open during two world wars.

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:39.551
Consequently, the fate of this class
convening on this magical campus was up in

00:13:39.551 --> 00:13:41.320
the air for a long time.

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:46.602
Eventually four cohorts rather than
the usual three were admitted,

00:13:46.602 --> 00:13:48.978
and the year kicked in to gear.

00:13:48.978 --> 00:13:55.131
First virtually and then in person and
here's the kicker with no MBAs in sight.

00:13:55.131 --> 00:14:00.620
As members of this pre-eminent school
of leadership your class ideated,

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:04.550
advocated and
negotiated the amazing Super Summer.

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:08.368
The most coveted MBA electives
taught just for you,

00:14:08.368 --> 00:14:13.250
demonstrating their characteristic
generosity and care.

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:17.190
The administration and faculty obliged and
showed up during summer.

00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:20.910
After all, so
much of leadership is about showing up.

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:24.660
You had 11 electives, wow.

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:27.541
When I was a student here,
we only had two.

00:14:27.541 --> 00:14:32.658
However, I must say that those two prove
life altering in Jeffrey Pfeffer's

00:14:32.658 --> 00:14:37.619
power and politics, among many
cognitions I learned that whistleblowers

00:14:37.619 --> 00:14:43.620
who risk everything to do the right thing,
are often feared and not trusted.

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:47.638
Small business with Jim Collins
planted the seeds of entrepreneurship,

00:14:47.638 --> 00:14:51.991
warned of people who go back and forth too
many times when accepting a job offer.

00:14:51.991 --> 00:14:55.678
And gave us lasting concepts like big,
hairy, audacious goals and

00:14:55.678 --> 00:14:58.600
having the right people in
the right seats on the bus.

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:03.952
You seem to have enjoy classes
like new ventures, touchy-feely,

00:15:03.952 --> 00:15:06.479
strategic communications,
pass to power and

00:15:06.479 --> 00:15:10.060
managing growing organizations
with your beloved Dave Datsun.

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:15.165
Moments of adversity present
our greatest opportunities and

00:15:15.165 --> 00:15:19.413
what may have started as a challenging
year for the MSX class of 2021,

00:15:19.413 --> 00:15:21.760
ended as one that was truly remarkable.

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:24.560
Now on to the future.

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:28.274
This pandemic won't be the last
world changing event that you will

00:15:28.274 --> 00:15:29.810
witness in your lifetime.

00:15:31.010 --> 00:15:33.853
In reality, it is only one of the first,

00:15:33.853 --> 00:15:40.180
the rate of change is accelerating,
but no longer in a singular direction.

00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:45.030
Historically we have experienced
one major revolution at a time.

00:15:45.030 --> 00:15:50.458
Our species became anatomically modern
about 300,000 years ago in East Africa.

00:15:50.458 --> 00:15:54.793
Around 50,000 years ago we became
behaviorally modern gaining

00:15:54.793 --> 00:15:57.800
the ability for symbolic thought.

00:15:57.800 --> 00:16:02.102
Around 12,000 years ago,
we have evidence of early agriculture and

00:16:02.102 --> 00:16:06.486
the first stationary settlements
around 5,000 years ago, writing.

00:16:06.486 --> 00:16:10.624
And mere 250 years ago,
the Industrial Revolution and

00:16:10.624 --> 00:16:15.523
the rise of capitalism during
the lifetime of many present here today

00:16:15.523 --> 00:16:18.745
in the mid 1990s, the Information Age.

00:16:18.745 --> 00:16:22.893
More recently, the lives of almost
everyone here have included the mass

00:16:22.893 --> 00:16:25.954
adoption of the internet and
the mobile revolution.

00:16:25.954 --> 00:16:29.090
You don't need to be
a statistician to see the trend.

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:30.754
As our collective knowledge and

00:16:30.754 --> 00:16:33.836
coordination capabilities
have exponentially increased

00:16:33.836 --> 00:16:38.040
the time between each revolution
has exponentially decreased.

00:16:38.040 --> 00:16:42.060
Today the speed has become so
rapid that we are in the midst of multiple

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:45.945
revolutions concurrently as they
are not all pointing towards and

00:16:45.945 --> 00:16:49.900
they are not all pointing
towards the same future.

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:55.073
Furthermore, not only are these
revolutions happening at the same time,

00:16:55.073 --> 00:16:59.096
they're also interacting with and
altering each other,

00:16:59.096 --> 00:17:02.400
resulting in highly
unpredictable outcomes.

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:07.544
You're all aware of big technological
phenomenon like the metaverse,

00:17:07.544 --> 00:17:12.528
genomics and gene editing, 3D and
4D printing and manufacturing.

00:17:12.528 --> 00:17:18.490
5G, autonomous vehicles, natural language
processing, voice interfaces and

00:17:18.490 --> 00:17:23.855
chat bots, cloud and edge computing,
blockchains and NF T's, Cobots,

00:17:23.855 --> 00:17:29.409
and robotic process automation,
which will affect every single industry.

00:17:29.409 --> 00:17:30.630
What about smart devices?

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:32.903
Smart used to just mean connected.

00:17:32.903 --> 00:17:36.884
Now it generally means powered
by machine learning algorithms.

00:17:36.884 --> 00:17:43.543
Smartphones use AI to improve
the quality of our pictures.

00:17:43.543 --> 00:17:48.116
A smart car will use facial recognition to
see if we're paying attention to the road

00:17:48.116 --> 00:17:50.610
and alert us if we're getting tired.

00:17:50.610 --> 00:17:55.095
Soon smart toilets will use computer
vision to analyze our stool samples and

00:17:55.095 --> 00:17:57.489
inform us of gastrointestinal issues.

00:17:58.570 --> 00:18:02.094
With IoT, universities,
hospitals and museums,

00:18:02.094 --> 00:18:06.899
whole cities in fact, can become
intelligent, proving easy access,

00:18:06.899 --> 00:18:11.237
providing easy access,
environmental comfort and security.

00:18:11.237 --> 00:18:14.067
Remotely or
autonomously piloted drones and

00:18:14.067 --> 00:18:18.690
unmanned aerial vehicles have changed
the face of military operations.

00:18:18.690 --> 00:18:24.607
We will see them transform search and
rescue missions, firefighting,

00:18:24.607 --> 00:18:29.556
law enforcement and transportation,
drone taxis anyone?

00:18:29.556 --> 00:18:34.382
On the life sciences side mRNA
technology of COVID vaccine fame can be

00:18:34.382 --> 00:18:40.140
deployed to address a range of
infectious diseases and even cancer.

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:44.650
We've been wearing continuous heartrate
monitors for a couple of decades.

00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:48.070
But now more and more these smartwatches
are becoming health devices.

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:52.492
Healthy people are wearing
continuous glucose monitors, and

00:18:52.492 --> 00:18:56.700
not too long from now, we'll see
continuous ketone and lactate monitors.

00:18:56.700 --> 00:19:01.479
I'm personally counting down
the years to continuous insulin and

00:19:01.479 --> 00:19:04.643
the ultimate sensor, cortisol monitors.

00:19:04.643 --> 00:19:09.643
Cortisol in forms of chronic stress,
which triggers immune and inflammatory

00:19:09.643 --> 00:19:14.264
responses, increasing susceptibility
to diseases like autoimmune,

00:19:14.264 --> 00:19:18.067
cardio metabolic and
mental diseases, as well as cancer.

00:19:18.067 --> 00:19:21.943
Multiomics integration,
where we combine wearable data,

00:19:21.943 --> 00:19:26.275
with data from exposome,
epigenome, microbiome, metabolome,

00:19:26.275 --> 00:19:30.539
proteome, transcriptome, genome,
screenome and other omes.

00:19:30.539 --> 00:19:33.730
Will deliver whole
person precision health,

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:38.974
where at scale we can predict just
about anything about a person's health.

00:19:38.974 --> 00:19:44.252
On the horizon we are seeing nuclear
fusion which if we can bring into

00:19:44.252 --> 00:19:50.377
reality will provide an inexpensive
unlimited zero emissions electricity.

00:19:50.377 --> 00:19:55.567
Cellular agriculture which produces
animal products from cells rather than

00:19:55.567 --> 00:20:00.615
entire animals can change the way we
produce foods like fats and proteins.

00:20:00.615 --> 00:20:05.930
Our increasing ability to understand
materials and control matter on a tiny or

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:09.634
nano scale is giving rise to
exciting new materials and

00:20:09.634 --> 00:20:12.226
products such as bendable displays.

00:20:12.226 --> 00:20:16.723
And inconceivably fast computers capable
of solving seemingly intractable

00:20:16.723 --> 00:20:22.110
problems we'll make our current state
of the art technology seem archaic.

00:20:22.110 --> 00:20:26.087
These combinations of
permutations are endless, and

00:20:26.087 --> 00:20:30.338
their outcomes unprecedented and
mostly unimaginable.

00:20:30.338 --> 00:20:39.150
Underlying and overlaying every single
one of these revolutions is AI.

00:20:39.150 --> 00:20:41.270
Itself the most
transformative force of all.

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:47.243
Machines will learn and
