that Dave is more than just a teacher.

00:38:12.700 --> 00:38:17.070
He's a mentor and a life guide,
whose closing remarks at the end of

00:38:17.070 --> 00:38:21.910
the quarter were described as truly
breathtaking and memorable One thing

00:38:21.910 --> 00:38:26.201
that makes this award so great is
that Dave was truly as excited and

00:38:26.201 --> 00:38:31.196
enthusiastic about his Summer Teaching,
as the students were about having

00:38:31.196 --> 00:38:35.970
him teach them long before Dave knew
he was going to win this award.

00:38:35.970 --> 00:38:40.249
He was raving to me and
others about his summer MSX mg sections So

00:38:40.249 --> 00:38:43.722
congratulations, Dave,
and thank you so much for

00:38:43.722 --> 00:38:48.122
all your contributions to this
class's academic experience.

00:38:48.122 --> 00:38:53.394
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; The late RJ Miller who was the Dean

00:38:53.394 --> 00:38:57.972
of the GSB from 1968 to 1978,

00:38:57.972 --> 00:39:04.124
Founded the certificate and
public management and

00:39:04.124 --> 00:39:09.430
social innovation program here at the GCB.

00:39:10.460 --> 00:39:15.675
The certificate program educates
leaders who understand societal issues,

00:39:15.675 --> 00:39:20.246
design for and evaluate impact and
understand the specificities of

00:39:20.246 --> 00:39:25.960
the management of social organizations in
both the public and the private sectors.

00:39:27.150 --> 00:39:33.833
In a world faced with dire global health,
equity and sustainability challenges,

00:39:33.833 --> 00:39:38.893
today's certificate programs
take the spirit of our GSB motto

00:39:38.893 --> 00:39:43.476
change lives,
change organizations change the world,

00:39:43.476 --> 00:39:47.772
to its full potential from
this MSX Cohort we have 11

00:39:47.772 --> 00:39:53.022
certificate candidates their names
are listed in the program and

00:39:53.022 --> 00:39:57.343
I offer you all congratulations
on completing that,

00:39:57.343 --> 00:40:01.085
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE] [APPLAUSE]

00:40:01.085 --> 00:40:05.200
We will be announcing graduation awards at

00:40:05.200 --> 00:40:10.931
a later time as final calculations
are going on as we speak.

00:40:10.931 --> 00:40:15.592
Those awards include
recognizing the top 10 attended

00:40:15.592 --> 00:40:18.673
the class as Robert L Josh scholars.

00:40:18.673 --> 00:40:22.938
Bob Josh who this is named
after has joined us today, so

00:40:22.938 --> 00:40:25.272
thank you for being here Bob.

00:40:25.272 --> 00:40:30.038
[APPLAUSE]
And about six or

00:40:30.038 --> 00:40:35.282
seven of you will have be attached
to Bob for the rest of your lives.

00:40:35.282 --> 00:40:40.219
The top student in the class
the person with the highest GPA

00:40:40.219 --> 00:40:45.170
in GSB classes will be awarded
the George GC Parker Award.

00:40:46.260 --> 00:40:49.852
George had full intentions
of being here today,

00:40:49.852 --> 00:40:54.847
I think he got his regalia was all set and
at the last minute was called

00:40:54.847 --> 00:40:59.245
away to a another meeting that
he couldn't possibly miss.

00:40:59.245 --> 00:41:03.816
He sends his regrets and
he asked me for an excused absence,

00:41:03.816 --> 00:41:07.381
which I'm going to go ahead and
grant him, but

00:41:07.381 --> 00:41:12.794
we'll be happy to announce the winner
of that award very, very soon.

00:41:12.794 --> 00:41:14.569
Before I hand over the podium,

00:41:14.569 --> 00:41:18.265
I wanted to just say a few things
about the MSX class of 2021.

00:41:18.265 --> 00:41:21.890
Since March of 2020, I'm so

00:41:21.890 --> 00:41:27.461
sick of saying unprecedented,
I cannot tell you.

00:41:27.461 --> 00:41:29.621
We throw that word around too much and

00:41:29.621 --> 00:41:34.359
there's a lot of stuff that's been
unprecedented, but it is an understatement

00:41:34.359 --> 00:41:38.066
to say the challenges faced by
this class were unprecedented.

00:41:38.066 --> 00:41:40.225
They were truly exceptional..

00:41:40.225 --> 00:41:41.027
As a group,

00:41:41.027 --> 00:41:46.503
you showed amazing resilience in waiting
six extra months to start the program.

00:41:46.503 --> 00:41:53.320
You arrived in the Bay Area at basically
the high point of the epidemic.

00:41:53.320 --> 00:41:56.803
And you did the first half
of the program with hardly

00:41:56.803 --> 00:42:01.428
an opportunity to leave your
apartments and meet your classmates.

00:42:01.428 --> 00:42:05.244
Those were amazing challenges and
you all face those and

00:42:05.244 --> 00:42:08.664
made the best of it and
we really appreciate that.

00:42:08.664 --> 00:42:13.862
Despite that, this class was an extremely
academically engaged group and

00:42:13.862 --> 00:42:18.973
you found a group of leaders and I want to
give a special shout out to Felipe,

00:42:18.973 --> 00:42:22.108
JY, Catherine, Nicole, Katya, Hannah,

00:42:22.108 --> 00:42:26.588
I've probably forgotten a few others and
I apologize for that.

00:42:26.588 --> 00:42:33.011
I want to give a special shout out to
all of them for their dedicated work.

00:42:33.011 --> 00:42:35.915
[APPLAUSE].

00:42:35.915 --> 00:42:40.008
That group I mentioned and
some others were dedicated advocates for

00:42:40.008 --> 00:42:43.033
all of you as their classmates,
they truly were.

00:42:43.033 --> 00:42:46.255
And they were wonderful partners
to the GSB administration for

00:42:46.255 --> 00:42:48.435
which we're very grateful.

00:42:48.435 --> 00:42:53.335
So I want to thank them and all the rest
of you for your flexibility and teamwork,

00:42:53.335 --> 00:42:58.470
to make the most of this very challenging
time and of your overall GSB experience.

00:42:59.600 --> 00:43:02.806
This is the end of the journey,
I know it was very different from what you

00:43:02.806 --> 00:43:05.390
anticipated when you
applied to the MSX program.

00:43:05.390 --> 00:43:09.147
I know that like any MSX class,
it's a transformative experience and

00:43:09.147 --> 00:43:12.130
your lives have been forever changed.

00:43:12.130 --> 00:43:15.376
And while all the experiences you
envisioned had to be altered and

00:43:15.376 --> 00:43:19.340
were constrained, I hope you will look
back fondly on your time here at the GSB.

00:43:20.550 --> 00:43:24.753
And I also hope you're going to
stay involved with the GSB.

00:43:24.753 --> 00:43:29.286
You're moving from the student
community into our alumni community and

00:43:29.286 --> 00:43:31.290
as I hope you've already seen,

00:43:31.290 --> 00:43:35.536
our alumni play an important part
in the academic experience here.

00:43:35.536 --> 00:43:41.811
And it's my wish that you too will engage
with GSB academic mission as alumni,

00:43:41.811 --> 00:43:46.772
give your time and
experience generously to future classes.

00:43:46.772 --> 00:43:52.158
I can say a lot more about what
the MSX program can mean for

00:43:52.158 --> 00:43:56.743
students, but
who better than our graduates to

00:43:56.743 --> 00:44:01.229
talk about their
experiences this past year?

00:44:01.229 --> 00:44:06.473
If I had to choose one word to describe my
experience, it would be Transformative.

00:44:06.473 --> 00:44:09.660
My one word to describe
this year is eye opening.

00:44:09.660 --> 00:44:14.740
A word to describe my MSX experience
this year would be great.

00:44:14.740 --> 00:44:17.000
Exceptional Unforgettable.

00:44:17.000 --> 00:44:20.850
My experience in MSX is filled with love.

00:44:20.850 --> 00:44:24.040
Family Growth Transformation.

00:44:24.040 --> 00:44:27.444
If there's one word that I can
use to describe my experience at

00:44:27.444 --> 00:44:28.850
the GSB is belief.

00:44:28.850 --> 00:44:29.450
Amazing.

00:44:29.450 --> 00:44:30.300
Deciding.

00:44:30.300 --> 00:44:31.210
Inspiration.

00:44:31.210 --> 00:44:32.380
Transformational.

00:44:32.380 --> 00:44:37.660
The word that I'd use to
describe my MSX experience is on.

00:44:37.660 --> 00:44:39.130
World opener.

00:44:39.130 --> 00:44:40.440
Life changing.

00:44:40.440 --> 00:44:41.660
Mind blowing.

00:44:41.660 --> 00:44:42.760
Exhilarating.

00:44:42.760 --> 00:44:43.830
Incredible.

00:44:43.830 --> 00:44:46.174
I came in with an idea of
what it might be like, but

00:44:46.174 --> 00:44:49.838
I've been constantly surprised at every
turn by the people that I've met,

00:44:49.838 --> 00:44:53.900
the experiences that I've had, and
just the overall energy of this place.

00:44:53.900 --> 00:44:56.308
Before I came, I was doubtful, but

00:44:56.308 --> 00:44:59.970
I am sure this was the best
decisions I ever made.

00:44:59.970 --> 00:45:03.897
This year at the GSB,
I've changed my definition of success,

00:45:03.897 --> 00:45:06.030
happiness and taking risks.

00:45:06.030 --> 00:45:08.650
The relationships both with my class and

00:45:08.650 --> 00:45:13.560
across the GSB are what has made
this experience truly spectacular.

00:45:13.560 --> 00:45:17.473
For some of us confidence can
be a revolutionary thought and

00:45:17.473 --> 00:45:22.247
the GSB community, students, alumni and
professors have been given me

00:45:22.247 --> 00:45:26.785
all the reasons to believe in myself
as they are my role models in their

00:45:26.785 --> 00:45:31.402
beliefs of making a change for
this world, It is the people,

00:45:31.402 --> 00:45:36.430
the students, the teachers, alumni,
that make this place so special.

00:45:36.430 --> 00:45:40.637
The thing that surprised me the most about
my time at Stanford was how humbling

00:45:40.637 --> 00:45:41.580
it can be.

00:45:41.580 --> 00:45:45.385
Now, there were certainly a lot of
areas where I felt that my talents and

00:45:45.385 --> 00:45:49.561
strengths were reinforced but
this place challenged me Unequivocally,

00:45:49.561 --> 00:45:52.706
most grateful for
the people that I've met here.

00:45:52.706 --> 00:45:55.297
I love GSB, I love Stanford and

00:45:55.297 --> 00:46:00.688
I love my family who strongly
supported me throughout the year,

00:46:00.688 --> 00:46:05.580
Stanford made my world bigger,
I enjoyed every single day of the program.

00:46:05.580 --> 00:46:09.378
Stanford has opened my mind to new ideas,
expanded my view of

00:46:09.378 --> 00:46:14.170
what I'm capable of and
connected me with lifelong relationships.

00:46:14.170 --> 00:46:19.638
But the MSX has meant to me, understanding
that there are no crazy ideas.

00:46:19.638 --> 00:46:23.849
The thing that I'm going to take away from
this experience is the Stanford mantra.

00:46:23.849 --> 00:46:27.248
It's to change lives,
change organizations, and

00:46:27.248 --> 00:46:32.200
change the world and I'm going to
do that in the health care space.

00:46:32.200 --> 00:46:33.630
I love you all.

00:46:33.630 --> 00:46:40.006
Thank you so much, it was an amazing year.

00:46:40.006 --> 00:46:47.285
